{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791068964,"nonce":"r8peEpIeM3b6TKavgjZ9Iofq+xg=","title":"Text baselines: align-items: baseline lines up box bottoms, not baselines, across fonts and sizes","message":"taffy 0.6 never gets a first baseline for a text leaf (compute/leaf.rs returns first_baselines: NONE, and a measure function can only return a size). flexbox.rs:1322 then takes the box height as the baseline (`baseline.unwrap_or(height)`), so `align-items: baseline` aligns bottoms.\n\nashui places glyphs as CSS does, baseline = top + half-leading + ascender for the face drawn (blinc_abi/src/text.rs half_leading), with the box sized from that font's line height. Bottom-aligning a 0.9em monospace `code` box with 1px padding beside 16px sans puts its baseline visibly high.\n\nReproducer: sh tools/snapshot/run.sh tools/snapshot/scenes/Controls.hx, then look at \"with strong and code\" in .ashui/snapshots/controls@2x.png. The `code` text sits above the paragraph's baseline.\n\nBlinc hides it by making every single-line box font_size x line_height tall and drawing at top + that font's ascender (blinc_layout text.rs update_size_estimate, blinc_app context.rs). That lines up only same-size text with similar ascenders.\n\nFix, handed to Blinc (blinc-b1): blinc_layout reports each text leaf's first baseline (top padding + half-leading + ascender of its face) to taffy, and containers carry their first child's baseline, so align-items: baseline aligns true baselines. ashui then drops nothing: UA rules already use align-items: baseline.\n\nRelated: c2b1713174f575218b40dcee3bbd3f2bff6dd6626d5be9b313edf91c41ee60cf (inline text flow), which shares a line baseline within one paragraph.","files":null}]}